d>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.88$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.28$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Countryside</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.12$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.72$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550842} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f6518b4-e34a-514d-90e9-c9eb50aaae11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551128}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1cf7f6b8-f438-52c0-a338-61f2ad7fa03e" :question/math-academy-id "q-135555" :question/problem "In a particular country, there are two groups of people: those who live in the cities and those who live in the countryside. A study has shown that each decade \n\n- $12%$ of people who lived in the cities relocate to the countryside, and\n\n- $28%$ of people who lived in the countryside relocate to the cities.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how these people change their preferences each year?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each decade: \n\n- $12%$ of people who live in the cities relocate to the countryside. This implies that $88%$ of them remain living in the cities.\n\n- $28%$ of people who live in the countryside relocate to the cities. This implies that $72%$ of them remain living in the countryside.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"2\">From:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Cities</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Countryside</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">To:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Cities</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.88$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.28$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Countryside</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.12$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.72$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.88 & 0.28 \\\\ 0.12 & 0.72\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124544 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abbdd778-7ace-5539-9d6f-cdf01804b237" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix Given Some Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "277522b5-e3dd-5b89-81f3-5cdba4469a16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550464} {:answer/id #uuid "77d648dd-908d-5044-81c9-f4c8de288371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550670} {:answer/id #uuid "98ceb55d-c397-5695-99ff-7995f7e2e05a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550755} {:answer/id #uuid "b6eebac0-9289-5154-9d7a-80de8f6fa66c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550867} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b44784-1307-5ab1-8d5a-2ec2e4bf1930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7b44784-1307-5ab1-8d5a-2ec2e4bf1930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550873} :answer-field/id #uuid "87636227-a251-5be3-befa-08c44f225fa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d2bfda5-1f22-5eca-90c5-42502b97859c" :question/math-academy-id "q-135564" :question/problem "There are three supermarket chains in a particular city: chain $A,$ chain $B,$ and chain $C.$ A study has shown that, each month\n\n- from the customers that prefer chain $A,$ $5%$ change to chain $B$ and $15%$ change to chain $C,$\n\n- from the customers that prefer chain $B,$ $25%$ change to chain $A$ and $25%$ change to chain $C,$\n\n- from the customers that prefer chain $C,$ $15%$ change to chain $A$ and $35%$ change to chain $B.$\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & a & 0.15 \\\\ b & 0.5 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.15 & 0.25 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each month:\n\n- From the customers that prefer chain $A,$ $5%$ change to chain $B$ and $15%$ change to chain $C.$ This implies that $80%$ of them continue to prefer chain $A.$\n\n- From the customers that prefer chain $B,$ $25%$ change to chain $A$ and $25%$ change to chain $C.$ This implies that $50%$ of them continue to prefer chain $B.$\n\n- From the customers that prefer chain $C,$ $15%$ change to chain $A$ and $35%$ change to chain $B.$ This implies that $50%$ of them continue to prefer chain $C.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\">From:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain A</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain B</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain C</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"3\">To:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain A</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain B</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.05$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Chain C</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & 0.25 & 0.15 \\\\ 0.05 & 0.5 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.15 & 0.25 & 0.5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.05+0.5=0.8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124544 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abbdd778-7ace-5539-9d6f-cdf01804b237" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix Given Some Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02c287be-ea57-55ce-baae-51bb45b38516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266167} {:answer/id #uuid "08deed52-4468-549e-81a6-f5ab7a3737e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266226} {:answer/id #uuid "1ac975b8-b27b-535d-a06f-1ef6ec9db9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266369} {:answer/id #uuid "50883166-e1a2-56c0-81b4-b76e3dee6317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266861} {:answer/id #uuid "db8543f6-e928-54f8-a113-98e22acbcee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50883166-e1a2-56c0-81b4-b76e3dee6317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266861} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed26647f-f52c-560b-b302-af5032a00378" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40ee85ea-08ea-5955-8652-e4607e79ae86" :question/math-academy-id "q-135566" :question/problem "There are three cable TV providers in a particular apartment block: provider $A,$ provider $B,$ and provider $C.$ A study has shown that, each year\n\n- from the tenants using provider $A,$ $80%$ swap to provider $B$ and $10%$ swap to provider $C,$\n\n- from the tenants using provider $B,$ $25%$ swap to provider $A$ and $25%$ swap to provider $C,$\n\n- from the tenants using provider $C,$ $70%$ swap to provider $A$ and $10%$ swap to provider $B.$\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 & a & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5 & b \\\\ c & 0.25 & 0.2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each year:\n\n- From the tenants using provider $A,$ $80%$ swap to provider $B$ and $10%$ swap to provider $C.$  This implies that $10%$ of them continue using provider $A.$\n\n- From the tenants using provider $B,$ $25%$ swap to provider $A$ and $25%$ swap to provider $C.$ This implies that $50%$ of them continue using provider $B.$\n\n- From the tenants using provider $C,$ $70%$ swap to provider $A$ and $10%$ swap to provider $B.$ This implies that $20%$ of them continue using provider $C.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Provider A** | **Provider B** | **Provider C** |\n| To: | **Provider A** | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.7$ |\n| **Provider B** | $0.8$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ |  |\n| **Provider C** | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |  |\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 & 0.25 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.25 & 0.2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.1+0.1=0.45.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124544 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abbdd778-7ace-5539-9d6f-cdf01804b237" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix Given Some Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9daa07dd-689b-5d68-a711-77459bc9f7e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122079} {:answer/id #uuid "c40ed3ab-fd7f-589e-9bca-e8611878bb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.07" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122080} {:answer/id #uuid "22e0d828-15f0-56a1-944a-243f28fd0241" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122081} {:answer/id #uuid "44d59735-fe69-523e-810e-154c352fc2f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.93" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122082} {:answer/id #uuid "45ca4e96-0cfd-54e5-a7fc-d0e7ec0255f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.99" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44d59735-fe69-523e-810e-154c352fc2f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.93" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122082} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3b787ef-0c6d-5613-ae18-c431681bcaa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f54c1f29-b43d-5f0e-a558-1fd0e7509f92" :question/math-academy-id "q-35791" :question/problem "There are three groups of fans in a certain town: those who prefer basketball, those who prefer baseball, and those who prefer football. A study has shown that, each year\n\n- from the people that prefer basketball, $32%$ change to baseball and $28%$ change to football,\n\n- from the people that prefer baseball, $45%$ change to football and $15%$ change to basketball,\n\n- from the people that prefer football, $25%$ change to basketball and $65%$ change to baseball.\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.15 & a \\\\ 0.32 & b & 0.65 \\\\ c & 0.45 & 0.1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the following situation for each year:\n\n- From the people who prefer basketball, $32%$ change to baseball and $28%$ change to football. This implies that $40%$ of them continue to prefer basketball.\n\n- From people who prefer baseball, $45%$ change to football and $15%$ change to basketball. This implies that $40%$ of them continue to prefer baseball.\n\n- From people who prefer football, $25%$ change to basketball and $65%$ change to baseball. This implies that $10%$ of them continue to prefer football.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\">From:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Basketball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Baseball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Football</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"3\">To:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Basketball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Baseball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.32$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.65$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Football</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.28$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.45$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.15 & 0.25 \\\\ 0.32 & 0.4 & 0.65 \\\\ 0.28 & 0.45 & 0.1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.4+0.28=0.93.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124922 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124554 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4821de45-1b6b-5b4f-be0e-96cf5395bc8d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a State Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6563e16f-667f-5435-9f47-0d26c955ed36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0.24 \\\\ 0.4 \\\\ 0.36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550614} {:answer/id #uuid "7f84ea8c-c7c9-5b77-8633-d538a890dd1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0.2 \\\\ 0.42 \\\\ 0.56\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550688} {:answer/id #uuid "a403bf17-2b48-55a3-a928-1f9b4c83a2d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0.12 \\\\ 0.52 \\\\ 0.36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550795} {:answer/id #uuid "bf55f709-9be8-5dd9-85dc-86bd8db6cd9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0.24 \\\\ 0.32 \\\\ 0.44\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550892} {:answer/id #uuid "d234ef89-b2e5-55ce-8aea-ffb54263f9df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0.28 \\\\ 0.38 \\\\ 0.34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6563e16f-667f-5435-9f47-0d26c955ed36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0.24 \\\\ 0.4 \\\\ 0.36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550614} :answer-field/id #uuid "9881a85c-e966-5649-976b-b7827ba47e48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27eeb3bb-6a91-5ba8-9145-47e0dfe56bb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-35842" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.2 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.3\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 \\\\ 0.6 \\\\ 0.2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{1}.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "To find the state vector ${x}_{1},$ we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.2 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.2 \\\\ 0.6 \\\\ 0.2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.24 \\\\ 0.4 \\\\ 0.36\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124545 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e93dde4-a8e8-548a-801e-3d9a320a4513" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix and Making a Prediction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "758ee170-1fcb-5640-8b61-f22fb7a21811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "520\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322063} {:answer/id #uuid "936daf2f-be59-5538-b600-77f0341e8b82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "400\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322316} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c760ab-015f-5f08-8419-73f7e6627df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "430\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322665} {:answer/id #uuid "ce8548e7-cae1-5bab-a94c-045833d4e0f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "480\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322760} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b6826a-9e7d-507c-8455-dfd824432ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "640\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce8548e7-cae1-5bab-a94c-045833d4e0f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "480\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322760} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe25491b-be23-5337-9805-76ec9cd44496" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62389cec-4c75-591c-8976-ec4ed362e628" :question/math-academy-id "q-35845" :question/problem "A certain company produces two types of smartphones: Phone $A$ and Phone $B.$ The following table describes how the number of customers changes between both types of smartphones each year:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Phone $A$** | **Phone $B$** |\n| To: | **Phone $A$** | $0.6$ | $0.3$ |\n| **Phone $B$** | $0.4$ | $0.7$ |  |\n\nThat is, $40%$ of Phone $A$ customers switch to Phone $B$ each year, and $30%$ of Phone $B$ customers switch to Phone $A.$\n\nCurrently, $600\\,000$ customers use Phone $A,$ while $400\\,000$ customers use Phone $B.$ How many customers will use Phone $A$ in one year? You may assume that the total number of customers doesn't change." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "From the table, we can build the corresponding stochastic matrix: \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe vector describing the number of customers for each smartphone is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}600\\,000 \\\\ 400\\,000\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(1\\,000\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n$$\n{x}_{0}=\\frac{1}{1\\,000\\,000}\\begin{bmatrix}600\\,000 \\\\ 400\\,000\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 \\\\ 0.4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the state vector ${x}_{1}$ after one year, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 \\\\ 0.4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.48 \\\\ 0.52\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one year, $48%$ of customers will use Phone $A.$ Computing $48%$ of $1\\,000\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n1\\,000\\,000\\cdot 0.48=480\\,000.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $480\\,000$ customers will use Phone $A$ in one year."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124554 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4821de45-1b6b-5b4f-be0e-96cf5395bc8d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a State Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5825d08-86a3-50d7-8984-8f2cd8d0faf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.393 \\\\ 0.607\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122151} {:answer/id #uuid "f9ad3b9e-20a5-5b74-9a37-9df7886cff6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.413 \\\\ 0.587\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122152} {:answer/id #uuid "2f7fb7ea-e2b3-5992-9bf6-e41c09e0cbb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.611 \\\\ 0.389\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122153} {:answer/id #uuid "491996ac-bf8d-5eee-a987-0588261d1f8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.442 \\\\ 0.558\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122154} {:answer/id #uuid "7b9686e5-79d6-5616-8acb-0e5b13b9ae3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.526 \\\\ 0.474\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122155}] :answer-field/id #uuid "98df5681-9ccd-5b69-82eb-39e17040c2c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da359ad7-2c5e-5f15-a2e5-6728987ffc41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.393 \\\\ 0.607\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391939} {:answer/id #uuid "a65dbb5f-4e7c-55d0-9006-3317ba92c5a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.442 \\\\ 0.558\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391940} {:answer/id #uuid "3ca1d74f-f9fd-556b-a80a-717911ef4cb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.526 \\\\ 0.474\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391941} {:answer/id #uuid "a42f9714-7fe1-502d-aca7-b5820479478a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.413 \\\\ 0.587\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391942} {:answer/id #uuid "e7837d5a-4a5e-50f1-b388-732ea129adef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.611 \\\\ 0.389\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a42f9714-7fe1-502d-aca7-b5820479478a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0.413 \\\\ 0.587\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391942} :answer-field/id #uuid "424b0520-f951-5a27-8a16-c0b8ff12cee2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f3da8136-058f-5b0b-abbd-f2c6d4a902e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-35846" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.2 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{0}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.7 \\\\ 0.3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \n\nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{2}.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "To find the state vector ${x}_{2},$ we apply two steps of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0},\\,{x}_{2}=P{x}_{1}\n$$\n\nAfter the first step, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.2 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.7 \\\\ 0.3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.29 \\\\ 0.71\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, after the second step, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =P{x}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.2 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.29 \\\\ 0.71\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.413 \\\\ 0.587\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124545 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e93dde4-a8e8-548a-801e-3d9a320a4513" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Stochastic Matrix and Making a Prediction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105e81b4-ebb0-52a8-aaaf-535d61ac1ba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,800" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550409} {:answer/id #uuid "3fc67c9e-b654-57e4-a474-667c5d454cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,500" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550514} {:answer/id #uuid "40c82cec-2aab-5e87-a7f3-187df9be1327" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550517} {:answer/id #uuid "76ffc93a-e662-59db-8132-6716efe1d93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,800" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550668} {:answer/id #uuid "9af91aff-676a-57a8-ab5a-633b6dcd682f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,500" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40c82cec-2aab-5e87-a7f3-187df9be1327" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550517} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2b5c355-cad0-5348-8dff-54a6b032b4f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "34952883-ed67-58e1-83a4-6ee369a6dde8" :question/math-academy-id "q-35847" :question/problem "A certain company produces $2$ types of flour, flour $A$ and flour $B.$ The following table describes how the number of consumers changes between both types of flour each month:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"2\">From:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Flour $A$</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Flour $B$</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">To:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Flour $A$</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"80\"><b>Flour $B$</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nThat is, $70%$ of flour $A$ customers switch to flour $B$ each month, and $60%$ of flour $B$ customers change to flour $A.$\n\nCurrently, $6\\,000$ customers use flour $A,$ while $4\\,000$ customers use flour $B.$ How many customers will use flour $A$ in one month? You may assume that the total number of customers doesn't change." :question/worked-solution "From the table, we can build the corresponding stochastic matrix: \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.3 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.7 & 0.4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe vector describing the number of customers for each type of flour is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6\\,000 \\\\ 4\\,000\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(10\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n$$\n{x}_{0}=\\frac{1}{10\\,000}[\\begin{aligned}6\\,000 \\\\ 4\\,000\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0.6 \\\\ 0.4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the state vector ${x}_{1}$ after one year, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.3 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.7 & 0.4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.6 \\\\ 0.4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.42 \\\\ 0.58\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one month, $42%$ of customers will use flour $A.$ Computing $42%$ of $10\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n10\\,000\\cdot 0.42=4\\,200.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4\\,200$ customers will use flour $A$ in one month."}]}
